{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Names and ownership only. Inject actual values from reviewed per-environment secret references; never store values here.",
    "Secrets are currently environment variables read by the application. Private env files are a portable example; use host secret injection after hosting review.",
    "Supabase service_role bypasses RLS. API/practice/maintenance are trusted services, not dedicated restricted SQL roles; narrower per-service credentials need a separately tested migration.",
    "All five containers use the same locked artifact but receive different secrets. Tutor never receives a database service key.",
    "Only the chosen provider receives a key; optional product capabilities require their own tested provider keys and explicit availability evidence.",
    "TUTOR_LLM is the shared factory selector for API, tutor and practice. Groq is recognized but refused in these production artifacts until its degraded privacy behavior has a separately reviewed launch contract."
  ],
